We just rolled out our most recent update to Voodoo Vince: Remastered. This update goes a little deeper than usual to address the issue some players have reported with the game not starting or running. It turns out the issue was mostly due to an incompatibility with D3D feature level 10.1 on certain graphics cards. VV:R now supports D3D feature level 10.1 which is good news for anyone with one of these:
 
• ATI Radeon HD 3000/4000 series;
• Nvidia GT 205-240/GT 300 series;
• Intel HD Graphics 3000/2000 (Sandy Bridge)

If you're running one of these older cards and you're still encountering issues, please let us know!

We also made the FOV slider official and added it to our Options settings in the Voodoo Shop! Feel free to try it out if you’ve experienced discomfort with the game’s default setting or if you just sit really close to your screen.

